b:
&gt; A fighter’s co-promoter is stating that he’ll be meeting with the Japanese fighter’s other promoter today to start discussions for a fight against a prominent boxer for May 2 at a major arena in Japan. The promoter will be in the U.S today for talks with the co-promoter for the fight.
&gt; 
&gt; 
&gt; The fight will take place on Sunday morning in Japan, and it’ll be shown during prime time in the U.S on Saturday, May 2. The city is 14 to 17 hours ahead of U.S time.
&gt; 
&gt; “I think that’s a great idea. We’re going to be discussing that tomorrow,” said the co-promoter when asked about his thoughts on the boxer fighting the Japanese fighter. “I think it would be a great experience for the boxer.
&gt; 
&gt; 
&gt; There’s no word about what weight the fight will be contested at. The boxer recently moved up to a higher weight class, and dethroned a champion. It’s going to be difficult for the boxer to move all the way back down to face the champion.
&gt; 
&gt; The fight between them could take place at a specific weight class.
